# Copy to .env.local and fill in whichever providers you want to offer.
# Setup instructions for each: docs/oauth-setup.md
#
# Leave a line blank or delete it and that provider is simply not shown on the
# sign-in page. "Continue as guest" always works, so none of these are required.
#
# These values are PUBLIC — Vite inlines them into the bundle, and every one of
# them is designed to be. OAuth client IDs are public by specification; the
# translation key is public by restriction, which is the difference and the whole
# of what keeps it safe (see below). Never put a client *secret* in here; this
# app has no backend and needs none.
#
# Netlify does not read this file. A deploy needs the same variables set under
# Site configuration → Environment variables, or the built app goes out without
# them.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_FACEBOOK_APP_ID=

# Google Cloud Translation, for the phrases Peri ships no translation for. The
# app's key, not the user's: someone who communicates by gaze should not have to
# open a cloud account before their board can speak Spanish.
#
# It ends up readable in the JavaScript, so RESTRICT IT — that, not secrecy, is
# what makes it safe to ship:
#
#   Application restrictions → Websites → https://aulitalk.netlify.app/*
#                                         http://localhost:5173/*
#   API restrictions        → Cloud Translation API
#
# A lifted key can then translate, from this origin, and do nothing else: what
# it costs is quota, not anybody's words. Leave it blank and translation is
# simply off — the phrases Peri ships still speak, because those are translated
# before the app is built.
#
# A referrer restriction blocks `pnpm translate`, which runs in Node and sends
# no referrer. Use a separate unrestricted key for that, in GOOGLE_TRANSLATE_KEY
# on the command line rather than in here.
VITE_GOOGLE_TRANSLATE_KEY=
